## 5. Headers (Academy 4-element)

  Every file in the count set starts with the Academy 4-element
  header on contiguous `//` lines: `// # ` (title), `// Logline:`,
  `// Setup:`, `// Beats:` with 3 to 6 beat bullets. Verified by
  reading the first 12 lines of each file in this session.

  Sample (x86_emit.oo lines 1-13):
    // # Emit Linux x86_64 AT&T assembly
    //
    // Logline: Folds hello.oo, emits SysV identity/rsi/cat/greet
    //         calls, or harvests println consts.
    //
    // Setup: fold, id/rsi/str matchers, collect_prints, and
    //        x86_emit_linux64 exist.
    //
    // Beats:
    //   1. Tokenize and refuse secret sinks.
    //   2. Fold hello.oo greet if the RBRACE-tight shape matches.
    //   3. Else emit SysV identity, two-arg rsi, cat bump, or greet call.
    //   4. Else harvest println consts.
    //
    // residual: Int args, 3-arg rdx, looping while, and AArch64 stay
    //          later.

  Same shape on every sibling: each one names its own role in the
  Logline, names the helpers it depends on in Setup, and ends Beats
  with a `residual:` line pointing at the next lane.

  Header counts on the 14 files: 14/14 have all four Academy
  elements. 14/14 end Beats with a `residual:` line. 14/14 Logline
  ends with a period. No beat names a line number, per dinner_lint.

  This board (x86_hyg.oot) also starts with the 4-element Academy
  header at the top of this file. It does not introduce a
  `residual:` line because HYG itself has no follow-on lane.

## 6. Leftovers / forbidden names

  The phalanx §6 line 137 says "No .py .sh .md .js." HYG searched the
  count set (and the directory of each file) for these extensions and
  found none next to the 14 x86_emit*.oo files. No `x86_emit*.py`,
  `x86_emit*.sh`, `x86_emit*.md`, `x86_emit*.js`. No hardcoded
  `/tmp/...` path inside any of the 14 files. The only `.bin.tmp.c`
  or `.bin` names that exist (from prior smoke runs) live in
  `ooda/.ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/`, which is outside the count set.

  HYG did not create leftover files. HYG did not delete adjacent
  smoke .bin or .bin.tmp.c names. Those names are outside the count
  set and outside HYG's lane.

